  "discussion": "A moderate, north-northwest swell will continue to decline tonight into the weekend, allowing surf to become moderate to small and then small. A new small, north- northwest swell will support continued small surf into Saturday before the arrival of a more significant north swell. This moderate, long- period north swell arriving late Saturday night may bring surf to advisory levels on Sunday for north and west- facing shores. Surf to at least moderate levels will last into Monday before the swell really begins to fade on Tuesday. A small to moderate northwest swell is then possible by next weekend. Surf along east-facing shores will remain rough and choppy due to the strong trade winds this afternoon, then may decrease slightly tonight and Saturday as trades ease early this weekend. Surf will increase again Sunday into early next week as trades restrengthen. South shore surf will stay tiny to small for the next few days, then a small long period swell could boost surf heights towards the end of next week.",
